# Repository Structure

**Project**: DSA Foundations in Python

> **📖 Single Source of Truth**: For complete and up-to-date repository structure, see [README.md](../../README.md).

## Quick Reference

**Key Directories:**

- `01_complexity_analysis/` … `07_hashing_and_problem_patterns/` – Learning modules (notes, implementations, problems)
- `src/` – Entry point and shared Python code
- `tests/` – Unit tests (pytest)
- `docs/` – Supporting documentation

**Key Entry Points:**

- `src/main.py` – Main entry point
- `tests/` – Test suite (run with `pytest`)
- Module folders – `notes.md`, `theory.md`, `implementations.py`, `problems.py` per README
